// test-error
// Issue #1183: a bool is not a number. `a / b` on two bools passed straight
// through to C, so a false divisor was an unguarded division by zero that
// DivisionByZeroAnalyzer (E0800) cannot see -- the risk is carried by the TYPE,
// not by a literal value.
//
// MISRA C:2012 Rule 10.1: an essentially Boolean operand is permitted only for
// the logical operators, for equality, and as a controlling expression.
bool a <- true;
bool b <- false;

void main() {
    bool c <- a / b; // E0807: '/' is not valid on a bool
}
